; Spiritual Weapon: a weapon of light that floats at the wizard's side, picks an enemy, rises into the
; air over it, swings down onto it and winds up again (scripts/SpiritualWeapon.cs). It is taken in one of
; three FORMS - an axe, a hammer or a sword - chosen on the page that follows its card the first time it
; is taken, and the form holds for the run (SpellData.Variants, .ai/decisions/2026-10-28-spell-variants.md).
;
; Everything a form decides is in its sub-resource below: its name, icon, words, numbers and level table
; replace the spell's when it is chosen (SpellVariants.Apply), and its milestones are its own
; (SpellEvolutionCatalog.SetupSpiritualWeaponEvolutions). The numbers at the foot of this file are only
; the template's, which no run ever plays. A form never changes the tags: every one is Arcane and Light.
;
; BaseDamage is ONE BLOW. BaseCooldown is the swing rate: every cooldown hands each weapon one swing,
; which it spends the moment it is over its quarry. BaseProjectileCount is the weapons. BaseRange is how
; far from the wizard a weapon goes for an enemy (it guards; it does not roam). Amount adds no weapon -
; each is a whole second attacker, as a Familiar's hound is (Player.FireSpiritualWeapon).
;
; Every table is written out in full so Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of its own, and
; no line names a size in pixels: an Area line is a share of the blow's reach (Player.FormatAreaLine).

; --- THE AXE: heavy and slow, the most damage a blow. It cleaves everything within reach of its quarry
; (SpiritualWeapon.AxeCleaveRadius) and knocks them back. Goes for the enemy nearest the wizard. It
; stays ONE axe: its table buys weight, never a second axe (Whirling Axes is where more come from), since
; every axe is a whole cleave and two of them out-damaged every peer by half in the balance bot. For the
; same reason its tags carry no ProjectileCount: Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps gives a spell with that tag
; and no count line a +1 at level 4 of its own, which is how the second axe came back the first time.
; One Area line, not two: a wide cleave is the hammer's, and the axe's reach is what decided how far ahead of
; its peers it ran. Level 7: 45 a blow from one axe every 1.2 s, reach +15%.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_axe_2"]
script = ExtResource("2_dcl2w")
Level = 2
DamageBonus = 3
CooldownBonus = -0.1

